  "_comment": "The kit's tiers and candidate models per provider. status: admitted (measured with the multi-provider-routing.md §4 protocol, or by an explicit owner decision recorded in `decision`), approval-only (never in a default roster; L11: it joins a roster only when the owner requests it with the task field owner_named and approves each launch), candidate (unmeasured), rejected (measured and dropped, see minutes). Prices are USD per million input/output tokens, standard rate, read on the updated date; they expire. The final choice per role is made by the harness installer reading this file. Router fields (R7, odd/tasks/model-router.md): price_schedule [{from, usd_in, usd_out}] where from=null means 'valid on the read date, start unknown' and the router picks the last entry whose from <= as_of; usd_in/usd_out mirror the first entry. effort_levels and effort_by_role use the provider's own level names. token_assumptions are Assumed (not measured) and are capped at max_context_tokens. launch gives the syntax per runtime; verified=false marks syntax never run on this machine.",
